1
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:01,600
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten.

2
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-eyed aunties who are a thorn in your side,

3
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning that corner over there,

4
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,820
and you'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

5
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:24,800
Over there is Kameari,

6
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:28,340
well, surely it's Kameari.

7
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:33,020
Everybody, come on over to our town!

8
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

9
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:37,720
The ring...

10
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:38,860
What's wrong?

11
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,500
I left the amethyst ring right here, though.

12
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,260
It's gone?

13
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:47,160
That was expensive, and now I'm in shock!

14
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:52,300
I lost my pendant here last week, too.

15
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:53,160
Me too.

16
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:57,320
Actually, I've been unable to
find my keychain since yesterday.

17
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,200
My underwear was stolen here.

18
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,660
Wait, isn't this a series of thefts?

19
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:06,340
But a thief broke into a police station?

20
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:06,780
Right?

21
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,420
That means it's an inside job.

22
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,960
The culprit might have
left some kind of clue.

23
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:16,200
It said so.

24
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:23,220
Hey, what's this?

25
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,420
Great Clash: Ryotsu vs. Crow

26
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,880
That's strange.

27
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:38,180
Hey, didn't you tidy up the
desk room without permission?

28
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:41,420
I didn't. What's going on?

29
00:02:41,420 --> 00:02:43,560
A part is missing here.

30
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,320
What?

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,060
We promised to deliver the finished
product to the dealer at the same time.

32
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,020
Go buy the same model kit.

33
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:53,060
Why don't you use that part?

34
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:56,180
This is a prototype of
my original model kit,

35
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,620
and there's only one of each part.

36
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:02,480
If we lose one,
all our hard work goes down the drain.

37
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,300
Isn't this the part you're looking for?

38
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,900
That's the one!

39
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,480
There, all done!

40
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,100
Just as I thought.

41
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:17,460
Why is everyone gathered here?
What's going on?

42
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,760
Kankichi Ryotsu, you're fired!

43
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,100
What on earth is going on?

44
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:27,000
Don't screw with me!

45
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,700
Why does it have to be me, of all people?

46
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,340
Your sixth senses aren't like Ara-san's,
you know.

47
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,560
Ever since the other day,

48
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,420
Just do something!
Anything, just do something!

49
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,360
You said that, didn't you?

50
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,320
That's nothing new. It happens all the time!

51
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:41,500
Stealing our uniforms

52
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,860
There's precedent for trying to sell them,
isn't there?

53
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:44,800
*Gulp*

54
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:48,240
No, that was for a charity bazaar, come on!

55
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:52,580
So the one and only model
kit part in the whole world

56
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,420
how did it end up in the
locker room at the police box?

57
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:58,740
I don't know. That's what I want to ask you.

58
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,320
Say it quietly.

59
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,980
Anyway, it wasn't me.

60
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,280
Why don't you prove your alibi, Senpai?

61
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,200
Right.

62
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:10,780
Well, this morning I went to Katsushika
Station to submit my apology report,

63
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,300
My ring was stolen this morning, too.

64
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:14,960
Just as I thought.

65
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:18,360
I don't remember ever going to
the police box's locker room.

66
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,060
Yeah, even Ryo-chan wouldn't
do something like that.

67
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:23,980
What's wrong?

68
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,360
The earring I left here should be here,
but it's gone.

69
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:31,240
Don't look at me. I don't know anything.

70
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:35,720
Hey, the wristwatch I left here is gone.

71
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,920
So don't look at me.

72
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,200
The tobacco shop on the corner is gone

73
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:44,660
How the hell would you
steal something like that?

74
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:50,580
Hey, come quietly and put
your hands out to be tied up.

75
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,660
Don't mess with me.

76
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:55,460
You arrested five people, you bastards!
This is a violation of human rights!

77
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:57,420
Are you still planning to play dumb?

78
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,840
You'd be better off
owning up to it honorably.

79
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,040
Shut up!

80
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:05,220
Alright, if it's come to this,
I'll track down the real culprit myself

81
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:07,780
and prove my innocence too.

82
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:22,220
Is this window the only way in from outside?

83
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,780
Not even a child's head
would fit through this.

84
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:31,580
So a break-in from outside is impossible?

85
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:34,560
Komachi, what's his deal?

86
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:37,520
He's just struggling in
vain because he's cornered.

87
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:49,640
So there's no sign of the culprit's
belongings anywhere in the room either?

88
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:53,360
So it really was someone from inside?

89
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:58,760
We will now question all of
you from the prefectural police.

90
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,900
Why are we the ones being investigated?

91
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:05,560
Shut up!

92
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,700
Doesn't the saying go,
"It's darkest under the lighthouse"?

93
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:11,440
Before you cast baseless suspicion on me,

94
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:14,740
Squeaky clean!

95
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,580
I'm warning you, anyone who doesn't
cooperate with the investigation

96
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:23,420
will be considered to
have something to hide.

97
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:24,940
Fine.

98
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:27,400
Let's settle this once and for all.

99
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,720
First, from the day before
yesterday until this afternoon,

100
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:36,420
we'll thoroughly investigate who
came and went from the locker room.

101
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,860
At 9:25 you went to the toilet,

102
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:42,320
and you returned to the locker room at 9:45.

103
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:42,780
Yes.

104
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,800
Twenty minutes is too long.
What were you doing in the toilet?

105
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,780
That has nothing to do with it.

106
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:54,760
At 15:28 you went to the
locker room alone. Why?

107
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:56,380
W-well, that's...

108
00:06:56,840 --> 00:07:01,360
Were you doing something you can't
tell anyone in an empty locker room?

109
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:08,460
My stocking got a run, so I went back to change,
you sexual harassment creep, Yabajun!

110
00:07:08,460 --> 00:07:10,600
My stocking got a run and...

111
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:12,140
Despicable.

112
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,360
Help.

113
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:20,600
Everyone's alibi has been confirmed, but

114
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:23,140
then who on earth is the culprit

115
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:25,640
...is it?

116
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,680
Have they found the culprit yet?

117
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,840
Detective Aki, now it's our turn.

118
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:34,900
You even called in forensics?

119
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:36,900
Just in case, the fingerprints.

120
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,420
I'm not the culprit.

121
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:39,800
Ryotsu.

122
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,720
Chief.

123
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,840
Actually, it's not just inside the station,

124
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:48,680
it's come to light that metal thefts are
also happening frequently at citizens' homes.

125
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,660
We've decided to launch
a full investigation.

126
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:55,380
You don't suspect me too, do you, Chief?

127
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,500
I don't want to suspect you either.

128
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,700
I really don't want to suspect you, but...

129
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,700
You already suspect me enough, don't you?

130
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:13,300
A lie detector would clear everything up,
wouldn't it?

131
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:17,080
Answer "no" to every question.

132
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,300
Understood?

133
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:21,100
Why do I have to go through this?

134
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:23,020
I asked if you understood!

135
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:24,520
Fine, I understand.

136
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,320
So, in the locker room,
the disrespectful one

137
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,660
has sneaked in before.

138
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:32,140
No reaction.

139
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:38,480
I'm the one who stole the precious metals.

140
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:41,500
No reaction.

141
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,620
That's a lie.

142
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:48,300
There, now do you understand?

143
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,680
Isn't the machine broken?

144
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:54,300
I've embezzled money for coffee before.

145
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,060
Eh, no.

146
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,100
It reacted.

147
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:01,040
See, it's not broken, is it?

148
00:09:01,040 --> 00:09:03,480
Yes, that's strange.

149
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,480
Enough already!

150
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,540
Damn it!

151
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,300
This is sickening.

152
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,480
Who on earth is the culprit?

153
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,300
Argh!

154
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:20,860
All the thefts happened during the
gap when Fukei left the locker room.

155
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,320
Aaaaaaah!

156
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:39,980
Damn it! So he was behind all of it!

157
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,260
Ow

158
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:00,800
Serves you right, you thieving crow!

159
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,460
My ring!

160
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,920
My necklace!

161
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,620
My key chain!

162
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:12,440
Mine!

163
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,720
What is the meaning of this?

164
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,520
Don't you understand yet?

165
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:21,500
So the owner of this nest is the
culprit behind the serial thefts.

166
00:10:21,920 --> 00:10:23,780
The culprit was a crow!

167
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:24,820
Crow.

168
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:25,900
Crows.

169
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:29,600
It's been all over the news, you know.

170
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:33,960
Crows have a habit of collecting
shiny things and unusual objects.

171
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,780
So the crow that stole the
model kit part from the desk

172
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:40,840
made a detour to your locker room,
and that explains everything.

173
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,300
Everything makes sense then.

174
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:45,180
So you're saying the crow stole all of this?

175
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,600
That's right.

176
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:49,700
How dare you accuse me like that.

177
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:54,380
You get suspected because
of how you normally act.

178
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,600
Yeah, it's your own fault.

179
00:10:57,400 --> 00:11:00,780
You call people the culprit, then turn
around and get defensive like this.

180
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:03,580
What the hell are you getting so pissed off about,
you bastard?

181
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:14,480
So the culprit of the theft case was a crow, you see.
Hey, look at this, there's even this stuff here.

182
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:22,780
Looks like it overlaps quite a bit with someone's specialty.
What's with that look?

183
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:33,900
You're blaming the crow for what you did, aren't you?
You went to all the trouble of a sneaky cover-up, didn't you? Is that right, Ryotsu?

184
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:39,500
If I were the thief,
I'd go for cash first, not junk like that.

185
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,600
Good point.

186
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,840
Nobody's had any money stolen, right?

187
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:46,740
So the culprit really was a crow after all.

188
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:47,940
Makes sense.

189
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:52,040
How dare you suspect me, Chief!

190
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:54,480
Even using a lie detector on me!

191
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:58,640
Sorry. That was hasty of me. My apologies.

192
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:01,440
Still, it's good we solved it quickly,
isn't it?

193
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,280
What do you mean "solved it quickly"?

194
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,360
Ohara, we've got a problem!

195
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:10,180
The doll we received from
headquarters is broken.

196
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,160
This is a disaster.

197
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:14,740
I forgot.

198
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:17,900
My remote-control toy
crashed into the window.

199
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,800
And I broke it.

200
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:25,420
If this was the culprit's doing,
it's truly outrageous.

201
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:28,480
If you come forward honestly,
I might consider forgiving you.

202
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:32,200
But if you intend to keep quiet,
we'll investigate thoroughly

203
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:36,680
and a strict warning and
disciplinary action will be necessary.

204
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:39,680
Because they fled in a panic.

205
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:43,580
Maybe some radio-controlled helicopter
parts are still left at the scene.

206
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,200
You'd better confess
honestly while you still can.

207
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,900
Chief, actually, that doll...

208
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,327
Chief,

209
00:12:50,377 --> 00:12:54,040
This might actually be the work of a crow.

210
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,520
A crow?

211
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:56,458
Actually, lately,

212
00:12:56,508 --> 00:13:00,320
there have been many
thefts by crows in the area.

213
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,800
That's right, the culprit is a crow.

214
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,600
I saw it with my own eyes.

215
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:07,600
The crow that knocked over
the scarecrow and fled -

216
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:08,840
Is that true?

217
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:09,420
Yes.

218
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:13,080
Just as I suspected, Chief.

219
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,620
As expected of the Chief,
what a brilliant deduction!

220
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:18,240
If it was a crow's doing,
there's nothing to be done.

221
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,620
Damn that crow.

222
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:22,800
Payback for suspecting me.

223
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,380
Alright then.

224
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,560
Ryo-chan, you're late.

225
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:43,820
It was a crow, a crow!

226
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:44,780
A crow?

227
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:48,760
I got attacked by a crow as soon as I left the police box,
and I've been running around trying to escape it.

228
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,520
That's why I'm late.

229
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,780
Reiko, are you still suspecting me?

230
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:55,860
Well, not exactly.

231
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:59,240
I hear crows remember people's faces,

232
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:01,020
so you should be careful.

233
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,480
This thing's handy.

234
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:08,500
My bed, that is.

235
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:13,720
A crow just sent that thing off
and flew toward the eastern sky.

236
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:17,400
But it's using chopsticks, though.

237
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:21,440
Crows are supposedly as smart as humans,
after all.

238
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,280
That's strange.

239
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,360
This month's cell phone call
charges have gone abnormally high.

240
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,720
It's a crow, then.

241
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:30,220
What happened to this?

242
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:31,880
It's the crow.

243
00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:34,600
The dango I left here...

244
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,700
Crow!

245
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,920
Who broke our window glass?

246
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,900
Crow, crow!

247
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:43,140
Crow, crow, crow!

248
00:14:43,140 --> 00:14:44,580
Crow, crow!

249
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,000
Crow!

250
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:50,960
Ryo-chan blames everything

251
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,560
on the crow, she says.

252
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:53,600
What do you think?

253
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,860
Since I pinned the blame on
a senior officer the other day,

254
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:59,580
I can't really say much, though.

255
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:09,800
That crow has been roosting
over there a lot lately.

256
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:13,060
Maybe it has something it wants to say to Ryo-san,
don't you think?

257
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:19,660
Uh-oh, everyone's already
starting to suspect me.

258
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:23,300
I need to pull off some kind
of fake evidence right now.

259
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,140
Oh no, the chief's
office has been ransacked.

260
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,000
W-what is this...

261
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,320
Terrible.

262
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,020
W-what on earth...

263
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,400
Please look at these footprints.

264
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,280
And these black feathers.

265
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:41,920
These are unmistakably crow feathers.

266
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:44,140
So, without even needing
to investigate further,

267
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:46,120
it's all the crow's doing.

268
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:49,900
But can a crow really move
a heavy safe like this?

269
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:51,220
Indeed.

270
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:54,140
Have you ever seen a crow up close?

271
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:56,920
They're this big, you know!

272
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,840
But these footprints are really unnatural.

273
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:01,960
What's with him,

274
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,800
that's the crow's strategy.

275
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:06,200
Can't you tell he's doing it on purpose?

276
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,920
There's a security camera over there!

277
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,780
Was that always there?

278
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:11,480
Well,

279
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:13,480
let's play it back right away.

280
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:17,440
A crow on the screen!

281
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:19,600
So the culprit really is the crow.

282
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,480
This is undeniable proof!

283
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,920
It's 120% certain, right?

284
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,440
But this crow...

285
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,900
isn't it moving strangely somehow?

286
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:29,680
It's as if

287
00:16:31,020 --> 00:16:37,240
it's stubborn! That's also the crow's scheme.
They deliberately act unnaturally to

288
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:41,260
confuse us. They're clever criminals.
Don't be fooled!

289
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:43,620
Aaaaaah!

290
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:01,420
Aaaaaaah!

291
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:14,320
Aaaaaaah!

292
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:16,880
Aaaaaaah!

293
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,680
Oh my.

294
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,920
My underwear...

295
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:40,860
Okay, one at a time, so don't push!

296
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:41,900
Wait, all of it?

297
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:45,400
All the underwear I hung
out to dry was stolen.

298
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:53,740
Some were even Bach brand, and worst of all, my bra got taken.
And nobody saw the culprit

299
00:17:53,740 --> 00:18:01,480
This must be the work of a seasoned underwear thief. I don't think it's the German version.
There are too many victims, one person couldn't do it alone.

300
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:08,580
Without any clues, the investigation will be
tough But I found this lying by the clothesline.

301
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:11,680
A betting ticket?
The culprit must be a horse racing fan.

302
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:14,760
I also picked this up on the balcony.

303
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:17,560
This is a pachinko ball

304
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,900
I found this at the clothesline too.

305
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,860
Isn't this a figure?

306
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,560
Senpai, didn't you have something similar?

307
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,060
That's a premium limited edition.

308
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:33,820
Of course, I have one too.

309
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:37,220
The culprit loves horse racing,
pachinko, and figurines.

310
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:39,340
Here's another one.

311
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,120
Hey! You're suspecting me again?

312
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,960
There are plenty of people
like that besides me!

313
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:49,920
Besides, didn't you just say the
culprit isn't just one person?!

314
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,960
E-excuse me, sorry.

315
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:55,480
Hello, hello,
what on earth is all this commotion?

316
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:58,760
Yes, sir! It's an underwear thief!

317
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:03,060
Underwear thief? Did all these
people have their underwear stolen?

318
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:06,840
Yes, it seems the entire area around here has been hit,
one after another.

319
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:12,280
And these guys are calling
me an underwear thief again!

320
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:14,160
Did you do it, Ryotsu?

321
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:16,640
Chief, what are you saying now?

322
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,900
I absolutely did not do it.

323
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:24,080
If you suspect me, search my room or locker
as much as you want until you're satisfied.

324
00:19:24,820 --> 00:19:26,220
Go ahead, look. See?

325
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:37,160
Why? Why would it be in my locker?

326
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:40,940
It was the same culprit, wasn't it?

327
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,600
No, that's not it.

328
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,260
It wasn't me! It wasn't me!

329
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,840
This is someone's conspiracy.

330
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:54,160
It's a conspiracy, this is.

331
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:58,300
It's him.

332
00:19:58,300 --> 00:19:59,740
Everyone, please listen.

333
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,700
It's the crow.

334
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:02,980
This whole thing is the crow's conspiracy.

335
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:06,300
You're still saying that?

336
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:08,200
But the crow...

337
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:11,240
Blaming everything on crows, crows, crows.

338
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:14,600
Nobody believes your nonsense anymore.

339
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,320
Stay home on suspension
until a decision is made.

340
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:29,900
Then that goddamn crow -

341
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,960
I can't take it anymore!

342
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:37,060
This calls for a head-to-head
showdown with that goddamn crow!

343
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:40,200
Assemble!

344
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:47,780
That's the one.

345
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:50,360
We've finally tracked down its roost!

346
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:53,340
So that's the delinquent crow that
messed with the senior officer?

347
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:54,140
Yeah.

348
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:57,240
Even if you told me to forget that face,
I couldn't.

349
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,800
It's fast asleep.

350
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,840
Let's wake it up!

351
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:06,800
Fire!

352
00:21:22,340 --> 00:21:24,200
All units,
we've been hit on the outside line!

353
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:27,700
We don't know where the crows are in this darkness,
so be careful!

354
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:41,100
Hurry up, hurry!

355
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:49,620
My light's been knocked out!

356
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:54,340
What is this road?

357
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:55,900
This is...

358
00:21:57,260 --> 00:21:58,740
This thing's got a huge rock, damn it!

359
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:00,020
Ow!

360
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:03,020
Whoaaaaaa!

361
00:22:03,020 --> 00:22:04,820
Whoaaaaaa!

362
00:22:04,820 --> 00:22:05,220
Whoaaaaaa!

363
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:06,540
Whoaaaaaa!

364
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,900
What do you think you're doing, Volbo?
I'll capture you all alive!

365
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:22,660
Eeeeeeh!

366
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:25,380
Aaaaaaah!

367
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:26,680
This is no time to relax!

368
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,360
Aaaaaaah!

369
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:31,460
Aaaaaaah!

370
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,140
Aaaaaaah!

371
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:32,900
Aaaaaaah!

372
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:32,960
Aaaaaaah!

373
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:33,400
Damn it!

374
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:35,700
Take this!

375
00:22:35,700 --> 00:22:37,000
Aaaaaah!

376
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,160
Aaaaaah!

377
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:41,920
Aaaaaah!

378
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:42,840
Aaaaaah!

379
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:43,420
Aaaaaah!

380
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:45,220
Aaaaaah!

381
00:22:45,220 --> 00:22:45,380
Aaaaaah!

382
00:22:45,380 --> 00:22:45,900
Aaaaaah!

383
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:46,420
Aaaaaah!

384
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:46,860
Aaaaaah!

385
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:49,840
Yakura is the best at this, by far.

386
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:52,740
And on top of that,
their numbers keep multiplying!

387
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:55,600
We have no choice but to run!
Floor it, Honda!

388
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,300
We're done for!

389
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:07,000
It's good that the crows stopped
tearing up the garbage, right?

390
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:08,320
Yeah, really.

391
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:10,940
Seems like it's not just Tokyo.

392
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:14,120
I heard crows have disappeared nationwide.

393
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:16,500
Where on earth could they have gone?

394
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:19,180
Maybe they found some
cozy forest to live in.

395
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:23,260
Speaking of missing, we haven't
seen Ryo-san around either, have we?

396
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:25,580
I wonder where on earth he went.

397
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,140
All right, looks like he's not here.

398
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:50,320
I can't take this kind of life anymore.

399
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,440
How long do we have to keep running?

400
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,300
No idea.

401
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,200
Ask the crow about that.

402
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:13,940
Draw on the eyebrows first,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash.

403
00:24:13,940 --> 00:24:19,540
A quick nap on the train on the way home.

404
00:24:20,580 --> 00:24:25,860
Another hard week,
the strain is only natural.

405
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:30,560
But I'm getting by with one hand.

406
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:33,260
A beef bowl with extra sauce,
soaked through.

407
00:24:33,260 --> 00:24:36,520
And the irritation from endless overtime,

408
00:24:38,140 --> 00:24:40,240
